                        "form": "буду/будешь… симпатизи́ровать"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c06958d2-36dc-33f4-9a04-87cd6e221d90",
                        "entry_id": "325002b7-a52d-3f73-9267-f8572f8aefac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "(кому?, чему?) испытывать чувство симпатии, хорошо относиться к кому-нибудь, чему-нибудь"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4430e4e-19c9-49ce-ac24-69ae82646556",
                                "sense_id": "c06958d2-36dc-33f4-9a04-87cd6e221d90",
                                "text": "При этом он может не испытывать к вам никакой вражды или может даже симпатизировать вам, это не имеет никакого значения и никак не отражается на его действиях по отношению к вам."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7220af5-d138-4be4-8920-b7cc7e3a2f7a",
                                "sense_id": "c06958d2-36dc-33f4-9a04-87cd6e221d90",
                                "text": "С другой стороны, с Саакашвили всё не так просто. Ему продолжают симпатизировать многие медиа, а самый влиятельный и профессиональный в стране телеканал «Рустави-2» и не скрывает общей с Саакашвили партийной принадлежности."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "601b98c7-f6dc-43ea-8fa2-785b077c0fcc",
                        "source_entry_id": "325002b7-a52d-3f73-9267-f8572f8aefac",
                        "source_sense_id": "c06958d2-36dc-33f4-9a04-87cd6e221d90",
                        "target_lang_word": "sympathise",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sympathise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "084df6f2-b2b6-3f28-b201-838868340a53",
                                        "entry_id": "5f969e2e-3c67-3b67-bb6f-b275760e4b35",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Non-Oxford British English standard spelling of sympathize."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "nonstandard"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dfe1f57-d3bc-4949-9c03-76abdcce4873",
                                                "sense_id": "084df6f2-b2b6-3f28-b201-838868340a53",
                                                "text": "Brown heavily sympathises with the challenges now being faced by his successor Andy Byford and Mayor Sadiq Khan, to secure a more sustainable funding formula for TfL that is less reliant on farebox income."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e16d553c-ea7c-4481-ba73-cf801b2febf3",
                                                "sense_id": "084df6f2-b2b6-3f28-b201-838868340a53",
                                                "text": "‘[…] who is to hunt up my witnesses? All of them are sailors, drafted off to other ships, except those whose evidence would go for very little, as they took part, or sympathised in the affair. […]’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8d6b4c2-14c5-4884-840f-95668df410ad",
                                                "sense_id": "084df6f2-b2b6-3f28-b201-838868340a53",
                                                "text": "And yet, though the happiness may be unenduring, what heart, though seared by time and worldly care, can fail to sympathise with those emotions of early life? In after years there are none such. They are the high noon of earthly joy. After them, life goes on decayingly and solemnly to its shadowy sunset."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8a88b02-9185-4c97-888c-b042f55f1443",
                                                "sense_id": "084df6f2-b2b6-3f28-b201-838868340a53",
                                                "text": "Dahl insisted there was no racist intent behind the Oompa Loompas but also said he found himself sympathising with the NAACP."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1ab40ba5-6e18-4715-91d7-ad35659c99a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "325002b7-a52d-3f73-9267-f8572f8aefac",
                        "source_sense_id": "c06958d2-36dc-33f4-9a04-87cd6e221d90",
